────────────────────────────────────────
The Four Stages (iki2li mini‑norm)
────────────────────────────────────────

1) Raw state – 1/0
●  ○  ●  ○
1  0  1  0

The pure impulse.  
No depth. No division. Just state.

────────────────────────────────────────

2) Division – 1/0 into 1/3
●──●──●
│  │  │
1  0  1

The impulse is divided into three equal segments.  
Comparability begins.

────────────────────────────────────────

3) Densification – 1/0 into 1/4
●─●─●─●
│ │ │ │
1 0 1 0

The impulse becomes finer.  
More points. More resolution. More precision.

────────────────────────────────────────

4) Comparison – 1s / 1/3 / 1/4 aligned
●────────────●
│   │   │   │
●────●────●────●
│  │  │  │  │  │
●──●──●──●──●──●

All three rhythms are aligned.  
Unequal processes become comparable.  
Transparency emerges.

